 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** $O(N \cdot S \cdot C)$, where $N$ is the number of pixels ($H \times W$), $S$ is the number of samples per ray ($n_{\text{samples}}$), and $C$ is the cost of a neural network forward pass. Batched rendering reduces overhead but increases memory usage [S1, unofficial].
-- **Memory Complexity:** $O(N \cdot S)$ for storing ray samples and intermediate rendering results. The `chunk` parameter limits peak memory usage by processing pixels in batches [S1, unofficial].
-- **Measured Performance:** Performance depends on hardware (GPU vs CPU), resolution ($H, W$), and scene complexity. Typical evaluations run on held-out test sets with 10-100 images [S2, unofficial][S3, unofficial].
+- **Time Complexity:** $O(N \cdot S \cdot C)$, where $N$ is the number of pixels ($H \times W$), $S$ is the number of samples per ray ($n_{\text{samples}}$), and $C$ is the cost of a neural network forward pass [G].
+- **Memory Complexity:** $O(N \cdot S)$ for storing ray samples and intermediate rendering results [G].
